# LAWS 2 AND 3, THE PERMIT, in the form affine-kinds decision 001 gives (note/project/term/affine-kinds/decision/
# 001-many-by-default-sole-and-hide-declared-per-form.md). They hold by construction, not by a claim:
#
#   no forged permit       `mark hide`: only this file makes a permit, so the one way to get one is `grant-delete`
#   every mutating route   the one public mutator, `delete-note`, takes a permit for the note it erases, and the
#   asks                   mutator under it, `bury-at`, is `mark private`. `mark sole`: a permit is spent once
#
# PENDING, 2026-10-20: `mark sole` and `mark hide` parse (compile/mint-bridge.ts FORM_MARKS) but nothing enforces them
# yet (check/hide.ts and check/sole.ts are affine-kinds-0007..0009). So a route in another file that makes its own
# permit, or spends one twice, still builds: see ../../twin/no-forged-permit and ../../twin/permit-reused. The private
# mutator IS enforced today (check/private.ts): ../../twin/route-skips-permit is refused.
load ./model
  find natural
  find person
  find note
  find shelf
  find flag
  find may
  find same

form permit
  mark hide
  mark sole
  link note, like natural
  link person, like person

# THE AUTHORIZATION TASK: the only maker of a permit
task grant-delete
  take actor, like person
  take at, like natural
  take whose, like natural
  like permit
  sift may(actor, whose)
    case yes
      back
        make permit
          bind note, at
          bind person, actor
    case no
      halt <Not allowed>

# THE MUTATING TASK takes the permit and nothing that names the target, so a permit for one note cannot erase another
task delete-note
  take s, like shelf
  take permit, like permit
  like shelf
  back
    bury-at
      read s
      read permit/note
      read permit/person

# bury the live note `at`, by `by`, with no check of its own: the permit was the check
task bury-at
  mark private
  take s, like shelf
  take at, like natural
  take by, like person
  like shelf
  sift s
    case bare
      back make bare
    case more
      back
        make more
          bind top, bury-one(top, at, by)
          bind rest, bury-at(rest, at, by)

task bury-one
  mark private
  take n, like note
  take aim, like natural
  take by, like person
  like note
  sift n
    case live
      back bury-if(same(at, aim), n, by)
    case gone
      back n

task bury-if
  mark private
  take f, like flag
  take n, like note
  take by, like person
  like note
  sift f
    case yes
      sift n
        case live
          back
            make gone
              bind at, at
              bind whose, whose
              bind by, by
        case gone
          back n
    case no
      back n
